# Trading Brains — TFT Price Prediction

Hourly S&P 500 (SPY) price predictions using a Temporal Fusion Transformer (TFT),
served via Cloud Run and retrained on Vertex AI.


## Architecture Overview

Polygon.io (training data) Twelve Data (inference data)
| |
v v
Vertex AI Custom Job Cloud Run Service
(pipeline/train.py) (main.py)
| |
v v
gs://tft-for-trading-brains/ BigQuery: tft_predictions_logs
tft_checkpoint_latest.ckpt
|
+-------> Cloud Run loads on cold start



## GCP Resources

| Resource               | Details                                                  |
|------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| Project                | `trading-brains` (137489665103)                          |
| Cloud Run              | `tft-predictions` in `europe-west6`                      |
| Cloud Run URL          | `https://tft-predictions-137489665103.europe-west6.run.app` |
| Serving container      | `gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-predictions`                  |
| Training container     | `gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training`                     |
| Model checkpoint (GCS) | `gs://tft-for-trading-brains/tft_checkpoint_latest.ckpt` |
| Predictions log        | `trading-brains.tft_predictions.tft_predictions_logs`    |
| Actuals log            | `trading-brains.tft_predictions.tft_actuals`             |


## Model Details

- **Framework**: pytorch-forecasting 1.6.1 `TemporalFusionTransformer`
- **Target**: `close` (SPY 1-min close price)
- **Prediction horizon**: 60 minutes ahead (quantile predictions at 15/30/45/60 min)
- **Encoder length**: 60 time steps
- **Normalizer**: `GroupNormalizer(groups=["group"], transformation="softplus")`
- **Loss**: `QuantileLoss()` (7 quantiles)
- **Hyperparameters**: hidden_size=32, attention_head_size=2, dropout=0.1, lr=0.001, hidden_continuous_size=16, output_size=7
- **Features**: 76 engineered features (returns, SMA, MACD, volatility, ATR, Bollinger bands, RSI, stochastic, ROC, volume indicators, OBV/VPT/MFI, VWAP ratios, time features, volume lags)


## Project Structure

trading_brains/
├── main.py # Cloud Run serving app (Flask)
├── Dockerfile # Serving container
├── requirements.txt # Serving dependencies
├── .env # API keys (gitignored)
├── pipeline/
│ ├── train.py # Training script for Vertex AI
│ ├── features.py # Feature engineering (shared logic with main.py)
│ ├── run_pipeline.py # Python script to submit Vertex AI jobs
│ ├── Dockerfile # Training container
│ └── requirements.txt # Training dependencies
├── temporal_transformers_exploration.ipynb # Original training notebook
├── prediction_logs_analytics.ipynb # Prediction analysis
├── trading_simulation.ipynb # Trading simulation
├── checkpoints/ # Local training checkpoints
├── models/ # Local model copies
└── readme # This file




## API Endpoints (Cloud Run)

| Endpoint          | Method   | Description                                    |
|-------------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|
| `/`               | GET      | Health check                                   |
| `/predict`        | GET/POST | Generate predictions, save to BigQuery         |
| `/test`           | GET/POST | Test model with historical data (no BQ write)  |
| `/record_actuals` | GET/POST | Record actual prices for past predictions      |
| `/backfill`       | GET/POST | Recalculate all historical predictions         |

Predictions are triggered hourly by a Cloud Scheduler job.


## Environment Variables

| Variable               | Used by       | Description              |
|------------------------|---------------|--------------------------|
| `TWELVEDATA_API_KEY`   | Cloud Run     | Twelve Data API key      |
| `POLYGON_API_KEY`      | Training      | Polygon.io API key       |
| `PORT`                 | Cloud Run     | Server port (default 8080) |


## Retraining the Model

### 1. Rebuild the training container (only if train.py or features.py changed)
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training --project trading-brains c:\Users\batzi\OneDrive\Dokumente\trading_brains\pipeline

### 2. Submit a retraining job on Vertex AI
gcloud ai custom-jobs create ^
--region=europe-west6 ^
--project=trading-brains ^
--display-name=tft-retrain ^
--worker-pool-spec=machine-type=n1-standard-8,replica-count=1,container-image-uri=gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training ^
--args="--polygon_api_key=IYHqABfrpYN6yfa7bFS9LLNxwJzpn0YE,--gcs_bucket=tft-for-trading-brains,--gcs_model_path=tft_checkpoint_latest.ckpt,--max_epochs=25,--lookback_days=425"


The job fetches fresh 1-min SPY data from Polygon, trains the TFT, and uploads the
best checkpoint to GCS. Cloud Run picks up the new model on next cold start.

### Training arguments

| Argument              | Default | Description                     |
|-----------------------|---------|---------------------------------|
| `--polygon_api_key`   | required| Polygon.io API key              |
| `--gcs_bucket`        | tft-for-trading-brains | GCS bucket for model |
| `--gcs_model_path`    | tft_checkpoint_latest.ckpt | GCS path for model |
| `--symbol`            | SPY     | Ticker symbol                   |
| `--lookback_days`     | 365     | Days of historical data         |
| `--max_epochs`        | 10      | Maximum training epochs         |
| `--batch_size`        | 64      | Training batch size             |
| `--learning_rate`     | 0.001   | Learning rate                   |
| `--hidden_size`       | 32      | TFT hidden size                 |
| `--attention_head_size`| 2      | Number of attention heads       |
| `--dropout`           | 0.1     | Dropout rate                    |
| `--patience`          | 10      | Early stopping patience         |

### Monitor the job

Check status in the Vertex AI Custom Jobs console:
https://console.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/training/custom-jobs?project=trading-brains

Or via CLI:
gcloud ai custom-jobs list --region=europe-west6 --project=trading-brains --limit=5


## Deploying the Serving Container

After changes to `main.py`:

gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-predictions --project trading-brains c:\Users\batzi\OneDrive\Dokumente\trading_brains

gcloud run deploy tft-predictions --image gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-predictions --region europe-west6 --project trading-brains


## Data Sources

- **Training**: Polygon.io REST API — 1-min OHLCV bars (free tier returns "DELAYED" status, which is fine for historical data)
- **Inference**: Twelve Data API — 1-min OHLCV bars (real-time for predictions)